  note = {Opened the Cambridge Core article page; open-access status not stated. Checked: standard GVS correspondences (ME ī > [aɪ] time, knife; ē > [iː] three, sheep; ɛ̄ > [iː] team, eat; ā > [ɛː] > [eː] > [eɪ] spade, bacon; ū diphthongized house; ō raised goose, moon); ā raising from the 15th century (citing Dobson), [eɪ] about 1800; Jespersen drag chain, Luick push chain resting on unshifted northern ū; Stockwell and Minkova (1988) dialect problem and the phrase "the linguist's creation through hindsight"; data from Kolb (1966), Survey of English Dialects; conclusion supports Luick, explains overlap by diffusion. Stockwell and Minkova 1988 not opened directly.}
